# Typographic quotes are not string quotes.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where s == “abc” or s == ‘x’
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..14
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..14
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "s"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        EQ2@12..14 "=="
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    ERROR@15..40
      ERROR@15..18 "“"
      IDENT@18..21 "abc"
      ERROR@21..24 "”"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      OR_KW@25..27 "or"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      IDENT@28..29 "s"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      EQ2@30..32 "=="
      WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
      ERROR@33..36 "‘"
      IDENT@36..37 "x"
      ERROR@37..40 "’"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `“`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | t | where s == “abc” or s == ‘x’
  |                ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: this is a typographic quote; use a plain `"` or `'`

